Restores the defect milestone 213 measured, which is the one the old phrasing of this
harness could not see: `read` slicing a whole directory span past where `parse` checked.

`start_block` is an absolute block number, and this crate's module comment says so ("a
reader never needs to know DIR_BLOCKS to find data; only the writer places it"), which
is exactly the sentence a reader could act on backwards. Adding DIR_BLOCKS before the
multiply reads as making the reader agree with the writer, and instead moves every
file's bytes a directory span past the entry the validation accepted.

Expected red: `an entry begins at its own block`, which states the on-disk layout rather
than the expression this function uses to compute it. Before milestone 213 the harness
computed both sides itself, and neither `parse` nor `read` appeared in it, so this
defect left it verifying in 0.04 seconds.
